    16	of M, reconstruct f_k = sigma_k * outer(u_k, v_k) flattened to length N,
    17	then for each modulus q in q_list compute the L^2 fraction of f_k that
    18	sits in the subspace of "functions of n mod q". A small Q* such that the
    19	spikes are entirely absorbed by V_{<= Q*} would identify the spike
    20	subspace as the residue-class character subspace; a "diffuse" pattern
    21	(no q captures > 50% of f_k for k > 1) would falsify (a) and push us
